# 7. AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORIZATION

Use Supabase Auth.

Roles:

- user
- admin
- super_admin

Registration:

- Public registration always creates a regular user.
- Never trust role values submitted by a browser.
- Users cannot modify their own role.
- Admin provisioning must be performed through a secure backend process.

Authorization:

- Public users can view published jobs and public company profiles.
- Authenticated users can manage their own profiles.
- Users can access their own resumes.
- Users can create and view their own applications.
- Users can manage their own saved jobs.
- Only administrators can create, modify or delete job listings.
- Only authorized administrators can manage companies.
- Only administrators can access all applications and user management.
- Only super administrators can manage admin privileges.

Implement Supabase RLS on every sensitive table.

Do not rely on hiding buttons or frontend routes as security.

Use database policies and trusted backend authorization.

